# 6. SECTIONAL EXAMINATION ENGINE

Support five sections of 40 questions and 42 minutes each by default.

The system must support arbitrary configurable sections.

## Section workflow

1. Start examination.
2. Open Section A.
3. Start its timer.
4. Allow navigation within Section A.
5. When section time expires, lock the section.
6. Open Section B.
7. Continue until all sections finish.

### Section lock rules

When a section is locked:

- Prevent further answer changes.
- Prevent response clearing.
- Prevent review changes.
- Prevent question navigation into that section.
- Preserve all committed responses.
- Preserve historical events.
- Do not allow browser refresh to bypass the lock.

A locked section cannot be reopened unless the examination configuration explicitly permits it.

### Critical timeout behavior

Define a precise policy for unsaved pending responses.

Default to discarding uncommitted selections in strict-save mode.

Do not silently convert a pending selection into a saved answer.

On section transition:
- Lock the expired section server-side.
- Commit any valid outstanding operations received before the deadline.
- Reject late mutations.
- Open the next section.
- Record the transition timestamp.

The backend must be the authority for deadlines and section transitions.

## Overall timer

Persist:
- Examination start time.
- Overall deadline.
- Section start time.
- Section deadline.
- Current active section.
- Lock timestamps.

Never reset the timer because of browser refresh, tab switching or device restart.

