# 13. PERFORMANCE INTELLIGENCE ENGINE

This is the second most important differentiator after the examination engine.

Build a standalone analytics service.

Do not calculate everything directly inside frontend components.

## 13.1 Overall examination analytics

Calculate:

- Total questions.
- Attempted questions.
- Correct answers.
- Incorrect answers.
- Unattempted questions.
- Score.
- Percentage score.
- Accuracy.
- Attempt rate.
- Negative marks.
- Average question time.
- Median question time.
- Total active time.
- Fastest correct answer.
- Slowest incorrect answer.

Formula:

Accuracy = Correct / Attempted × 100.

Attempt Rate = Attempted / Total Questions × 100.

Score = Correct × Positive Marks − Incorrect × Negative Marks.

All calculations must use the examination's stored scoring configuration.

## 13.2 Subject-wise analysis

For every subject calculate:

- Total questions.
- Attempted.
- Correct.
- Incorrect.
- Unattempted.
- Accuracy.
- Attempt rate.
- Marks earned.
- Marks lost.
- Average time.
- Median time.
- Guess percentage.
- Main Guess accuracy.
- Second Guess accuracy.
- Sure accuracy.

Provide sorting and drill-down.

## 13.3 Topic-wise analysis

Hierarchy:

Subject → System → Topic → Subtopic.

Identify:

- Strong topics.
- Weak topics.
- Frequently incorrect topics.
- High-time-consumption topics.
- High-guess-frequency topics.
- Repeated conceptual errors.
- Declining performance.
- Low attempt rate.

## 13.4 Speed and accuracy matrix

Classify:

| Accuracy | Speed | Interpretation |
|---|---|---|
| High | Fast | Strong mastery |
| High | Slow | Knowledge exists, speed needs work |
| Low | Fast | Possible superficial understanding or careless mistakes |
| Low | Slow | Priority revision |

Thresholds must be configurable.

Do not make strong conclusions from small question samples.

## 13.5 Knowledge gap detection

Calculate a transparent knowledge-gap score using configurable factors:

- Incorrect frequency.
- Recent incorrect answers.
- Repeated concept errors.
- Low accuracy.
- High time consumption.
- Guess dependency.
- Retention failures.
- Negative marking impact.

Store the formula version.

Show why a topic is classified as weak.

Do not use an unexplained black-box score.

## 13.6 Performance trend analysis

Compare:

- Last 3 mock tests.
- Last 5 mock tests.
- Last 10 mock tests.
- All mock tests.
- Custom date range.

Display:

- Score progression.
- Accuracy progression.
- Speed progression.
- Subject-wise improvement.
- Guessing accuracy.
- Negative marks.
- Weakness reduction.

Use historical snapshots, not recalculated historical data.

